Subject: [PATCH 06/12] Tier 2 #6: Audit log table + middleware + /api/audit
 endpoint

Adds an audit_log table (id, at, action, method, path, user, source_ip, params,
status_code, detail) and instruments the four state-changing API calls:

  POST /api/refresh    - background ingest trigger (records start / already-running)
  POST /api/demo       - synthetic data load (records refusal if real data exists)
  POST /api/upload     - CSV/XLSX upload (records series_id, filename, rows, replace, status)
  POST /api/scenario   - scenario computation (records shocks, horizon, status)

GET /api/audit exposes the most recent N (default 100, max 500) entries. This
endpoint is exempted from Basic Auth alongside /api/health and /api/security,
since audit data is operational metadata, not market data.

The middleware now opens three paths: /api/health (Render checks), /api/security
(auth posture), /api/audit (operator review). All others still require auth when
ZTI_PASSWORD is set.

72 tests passing (1 new).
